        </presetGroup>
        <opcodeList>
          <udo>
            <style>MODERN</style>
            <opcodeName>blep_diff</opcodeName>
            <outTypes>k</outTypes>
            <inputArguments>kd</inputArguments>
            <codeBody>kout init 0

if kd &lt; 1.0 then
    kout = ((((0.125 * kd) - 0.3333333333333333) * kd - 0.25) * kd + 1.0) * kd - 0.5
elseif kd &lt; 2.0 then
    kout = ((((-0.04166666666666666 * kd) + 0.3333333333333333) * kd - 0.9166666666666666) * kd + 1.0) * kd - 0.3333333333333333
else
    kout = 0.0
endif

xout kout</codeBody>
            <comments>BLEP difference polynomial from Gabrielli/D'Angelo/Squartini, "Antialiasing in BBD Chips Using BLEP" (DAFx-25, 2025), matching D'Angelo's reference implementation bbd_blep.m: first branch for d &lt; 1, second for 1 &lt;= d &lt; 2, zero for d &gt;= 2.</comments>
          </udo>
          <udo>
            <style>MODERN</style>
            <opcodeName>bbd_line</opcodeName>
            <outTypes>a</outTypes>
            <inputArguments>ain, afclk, i_stages</inputArguments>
            <codeBody>i_cells = int(i_stages / 2)
k_buf[] init i_cells
kphasor init 0
kwrite_ptr init 0
kx_prev init 0
kz1 init 0
kz2 init 0
aout init 0

kindx = 0
while kindx &lt; ksmps do
    kin = ain[kindx]
    kfclk = afclk[kindx]
    kinc = kfclk / sr
    kinv_inc = 1.0 / kinc

    kphasor = kphasor + kinc
    while kphasor &gt;= 1.0 do
        kz2 = kz1
        kz1 = k_buf[kwrite_ptr]

        kdt = (kinv_inc * (1.0 - kphasor)) + 1.0
        k_buf[kwrite_ptr] = (kdt * (kin - kx_prev)) + kx_prev

        kwrite_ptr = (kwrite_ptr + 1) % i_cells
        kphasor = kphasor - 1.0
    od

    ky = k_buf[kwrite_ptr]
    kzm1 = k_buf[(kwrite_ptr + 1) % i_cells]
    kzm2 = k_buf[(kwrite_ptr + 2) % i_cells]

    kd1 = kphasor * kinv_inc
    kd2 = kd1 + kinv_inc
    kdm1 = (1.0 - kphasor) * kinv_inc
    kdm2 = kdm1 + kinv_inc

    ; At sr=44100, the highest BBD clock is 36469 Hz (31250 * 1.167), so
    ; kinv_inc = sr/fclk never falls below 1. kd1 &gt;= 0 therefore makes
    ; kd3 and kdm3 &gt;= 2, where blep_diff is zero. Omit those third-neighbor
    ; calls and their unused state/array reads.
    kcorr = ((kz1 - ky) * blep_diff(kd1)) + \
            ((kz2 - kz1) * blep_diff(kd2)) + \
            ((kzm1 - ky) * blep_diff(kdm1)) + \
            ((kzm2 - kzm1) * blep_diff(kdm2))

    aout[kindx] = ky - kcorr
    kx_prev = kin

    kindx += 1
od
xout aout

/* Previous bbd_line implementation, retained for comparison:
i_cells = int(i_stages / 2)
k_buf[] init i_cells
kphasor init 0
kwrite_ptr init 0
kx_prev init 0
kz1 init 0
kz2 init 0
kz3 init 0
aout init 0

kindx = 0
while kindx &lt; ksmps do
    kin = ain[kindx]
    kfclk = afclk[kindx]
    kinc = kfclk / sr
    kinv_inc = 1.0 / kinc

    kphasor = kphasor + kinc
    while kphasor &gt;= 1.0 do
        kz3 = kz2
        kz2 = kz1
        kz1 = k_buf[kwrite_ptr]

        kdt = (kinv_inc * (1.0 - kphasor)) + 1.0
        k_buf[kwrite_ptr] = (kdt * (kin - kx_prev)) + kx_prev

        kwrite_ptr = (kwrite_ptr + 1) % i_cells
        kphasor = kphasor - 1.0
    od

    ky = k_buf[kwrite_ptr]
    kzm1 = k_buf[(kwrite_ptr + 1) % i_cells]
    kzm2 = k_buf[(kwrite_ptr + 2) % i_cells]
    kzm3 = k_buf[(kwrite_ptr + 3) % i_cells]

    kd1 = kphasor * kinv_inc
    kd2 = kd1 + kinv_inc
    kd3 = kd2 + kinv_inc
    kdm1 = (1.0 - kphasor) * kinv_inc
    kdm2 = kdm1 + kinv_inc
    kdm3 = kdm2 + kinv_inc

    kcorr = ((kz1 - ky) * blep_diff(kd1)) + \
            ((kz2 - kz1) * blep_diff(kd2)) + \
            ((kz3 - kz2) * blep_diff(kd3)) + \
            ((kzm1 - ky) * blep_diff(kdm1)) + \
            ((kzm2 - kzm1) * blep_diff(kdm2)) + \
            ((kzm3 - kzm2) * blep_diff(kdm3))

    aout[kindx] = ky - kcorr
    kx_prev = kin

    kindx += 1
od
xout aout
*/</codeBody>
            <comments>Sample-by-sample BBD line after D'Angelo's bbd_blep.m (DAFx-25 companion): interpolated write, forward/backward neighbour BLEP corrections. Third-neighbour terms omitted: kinv_inc = sr/fclk &gt;= 1.209 for the Juno clock range (max 36469 Hz at sr 44100), so d3/dm3 &gt;= 2 where blep_diff is zero. Charge leakage, nonlinearities and noise are out of scope per the reference implementation.</comments>
          </udo>
          <udo>
            <style>MODERN</style>
            <opcodeName>juno_bbd_encode</opcodeName>
            <outTypes>a</outTypes>
            <inputArguments>ain</inputArguments>
            <codeBody>; Unity small-signal gain: tanh(x*k)/k is unity for any k, so the wet/dry
; balance does not depend on the input level. Drive k = 0.4 puts the measured
; wet-path THD at 0.28% (1 kHz, LFO static), matching the ~0.25% harmonic
; distortion Raffel/Smith (DAFx-10, 2010) report for a 256-stage BBD
; (about 1.01*N/1024 percent).
xout tanh(ain * 0.4) / 0.4</codeBody>
            <comments>Compander-like input drive before the BBD, following Raffel/Smith, "Modelling, Analysis and Simulation of Bucket Brigade Device Circuits" (DAFx-10, 2010), section 3.2. tanh with unity small-signal gain (tanh(x*k)/k, any k). Drive k=0.4 gives a measured wet-path THD of 0.28% (1 kHz, LFO static), matching the ~0.25% chip distortion reported for a 256-stage BBD (1.01*N/1024 %). No expander after the BBD - chorus circuits are generally modelled without companding (section 3.1) and the Holters/Parker Juno-60 model has none.</comments>
          </udo>
          <udo>
            <style>MODERN</style>
            <opcodeName>juno_bbd_infilter</opcodeName>
            <outTypes>a</outTypes>
            <inputArguments>ain</inputArguments>
            <codeBody>; Juno-60 chorus input filter: 5th-order low-pass.
; Poles measured on a real Juno-60 by Holters/Parker (DAFx-18, Table 1):
; 7413 Hz (real pole), 9691 Hz Q0.549, 10345 Hz Q1.237.
; Replaces tone(..., 6800), which was only 6 dB/oct and let strong aliasing
; through (an 18 kHz input folded at -41.7 dB; now -78 dB).
a1 = tone(ain, 7413)
a1 = zdf2pole(a1, 9691, 0.549, 0)
a1 = zdf2pole(a1, 10345, 1.237, 0)
xout a1</codeBody>
            <comments>Juno-60 chorus input filter: 5th-order low-pass. Poles measured on a real Juno-60 by Holters/Parker, "A Combined Model for a Bucket Brigade Device and its Input and Output Filters" (DAFx-18, 2018), Table 1: 7413 Hz (real pole), 9691 Hz Q0.549, 10345 Hz Q1.237. The bias-adjustment high-pass of the real circuit is excluded, as in the paper's own model.</comments>
          </udo>
          <udo>
            <style>MODERN</style>
            <opcodeName>juno_bbd_decode</opcodeName>
            <outTypes>a</outTypes>
            <inputArguments>ain</inputArguments>
            <codeBody>; Juno-60 chorus output filter: 5th-order low-pass.
; Poles measured on a real Juno-60 by Holters/Parker (DAFx-18, Table 1):
; 8873 Hz Q0.542, 10381 Hz Q1.241, real pole 28053 Hz.
a1 = zdf2pole(ain, 8873, 0.542, 0)
a1 = zdf2pole(a1, 10381, 1.241, 0)
a1 = tone(a1, 28053)

; DC block; the bias high-pass of the real circuit is not modelled.
xout atone(a1, 20)</codeBody>
            <comments>Juno-60 chorus output filter: 5th-order low-pass. Poles measured on a real Juno-60 by Holters/Parker (DAFx-18, 2018), Table 1: 8873 Hz Q0.542, 10381 Hz Q1.241, real pole 28053 Hz. The circuit bias high-pass is not modelled; a 20 Hz DC block stands in for it.</comments>
          </udo>
          <udo>
            <style>MODERN</style>
            <opcodeName>juno_vintage_character</opcodeName>
            <outTypes>a</outTypes>
            <inputArguments>ain, afclk, kamount</inputArguments>
            <codeBody>aclock = poscil:a(0.0008, afclk, -1, 0)
aclock = atone(aclock, 7000)
ahiss = rand:a(0.0012)
ahiss = buthp(ahiss, 2500)
    
xout ain + ((aclock + (ahiss * 0.45)) * kamount)</codeBody>
            <comments>Optional vintage coloration: clock feedthrough tone at the BBD clock rate (a known non-ideal effect named by Gabrielli et al., DAFx-25) plus band-limited hiss, following Raffel/Smith (DAFx-10, 2010), section 4.3 "Modeling BBD Noise". Added at the BBD output, before juno_bbd_decode, so the output filter shapes both (noise "immediately before or after the delay line", Raffel/Smith). At sr 44100 the 26-36.5 kHz clock tone aliases into the audio band.</comments>
          </udo>
          <udo>
            <style>MODERN</style>
            <opcodeName>juno_chorus</opcodeName>
            <outTypes>a, a</outTypes>
            <inputArguments>asig_in, kmode, kvintage</inputArguments>
            <codeBody>; Juno chorus: 2 x MN3009. The MN3009 is a 256-stage chip, so the delay
; line has 128 cells. (Was 512 - i.e. 256 cells: a different chip and
; twice the real delay.)
i_stages = 256
; 128 / 31250 = 4.10 ms base delay. At kdepth 0.167 the clock spans
; 26.0-36.5 kHz; 26 kHz is the minimum BBD clock measured on a real
; Juno-60 (Holters/Parker, DAFx-18), which puts the max delay at 4.92 ms.
; The clock stays below sr, so the 3rd-neighbour terms dropped in
; bbd_line remain zero.
ibase_fclk = 31250

; Front-panel settings (Anwander's Roland chorus survey; the SoundForce
; Chorus 6 manual quotes the same four numbers):
;   I            = 100% amount, 0.5 Hz, triangle, inverted between channels
;   II           = 100% amount, 0.8 Hz, triangle, inverted between channels
;   I+II Juno-60 =   8% amount, 1 Hz, sine, no inversion -&gt; no stereo spread
;   I+II Juno-6  =  25% amount, 8 Hz, sine, no inversion -&gt; no stereo spread
kdepth_1 = 0.167
krate_1 = 0.50
kdepth_2 = 0.167
krate_2 = 0.80
kdepth_60 = 0.0134
krate_60 = 1.0
kdepth_6 = 0.0418
krate_6 = 8.0

; Hardware mixes the dry signal 1:1 into both BBD outputs.
kwet = 0.5
kdry = 0.5

if kmode &lt; 1 then
    kmode = 1
endif
if kvintage &lt; 0 then
    kvintage = 0
endif
if kvintage &gt; 1 then
    kvintage = 1
endif

abbd_in = juno_bbd_infilter(juno_bbd_encode(asig_in))

if kmode &lt; 1.5 then
    ; Mode I: triangle LFO, 180 degrees apart between the channels.
    aph = phasor:a(krate_1)
    amod_l = kdepth_1 * (1.0 - (4.0 * abs(aph - 0.5)))
    amod_r = kdepth_1 * (1.0 - (4.0 * abs(frac(aph + 0.5) - 0.5)))
elseif kmode &lt; 2.5 then
    ; Mode II: same amount, slightly faster.
    aph = phasor:a(krate_2)
    amod_l = kdepth_2 * (1.0 - (4.0 * abs(aph - 0.5)))
    amod_r = kdepth_2 * (1.0 - (4.0 * abs(frac(aph + 0.5) - 0.5)))
elseif kmode &lt; 3.5 then
    ; I + II (Juno 60): slow sine, channels in phase, no stereo spread.
    amod_l = poscil:a(kdepth_60, krate_60, -1, 0.0)
    amod_r = amod_l
else
    ; I + II (Juno 6): fast sine vibrato, channels in phase.
    amod_l = poscil:a(kdepth_6, krate_6, -1, 0.0)
    amod_r = amod_l
endif

afclk_l = ibase_fclk * (1.0 + amod_l)
afclk_r = ibase_fclk * (1.0 + amod_r)

awet_l = bbd_line(abbd_in, afclk_l, i_stages)
awet_r = bbd_line(abbd_in, afclk_r, i_stages)

awet_l = juno_vintage_character(awet_l, afclk_l, kvintage)
awet_r = juno_vintage_character(awet_r, afclk_r, kvintage)

awet_l = juno_bbd_decode(awet_l)
awet_r = juno_bbd_decode(awet_r)

; Dry centred, wet motion split across the stereo field.
xout (asig_in * kdry) + (awet_l * kwet), (asig_in * kdry) + (awet_r * kwet)</codeBody>
            <comments>Juno stereo chorus: 2 x MN3009 (256 stages, 128 cells, 4.10 ms @ 31250 Hz; clock 26.0-36.5 kHz -&gt; 3.51-4.92 ms, with 26 kHz the measured Juno-60 minimum, Holters/Parker DAFx-18). Front-panel LFO settings from Anwander's Roland chorus survey and the SoundForce Chorus 6 manual: I 0.5 Hz / II 0.8 Hz triangle, 180 deg between channels; I+II 1 Hz 8% sine (Juno 60) and 8 Hz 25% sine (Juno 6), channels in phase. Dry mixed 1:1 into both BBD outputs as in the hardware. See juno_bbd_encode (Raffel/Smith DAFx-10 3.2), juno_vintage_character (4.3), filters (Holters/Parker DAFx-18 Table 1), bbd_line (DAFx-25).</comments>
          </udo>
        </opcodeList>
      </instrument>
    </instrumentAssignment>
    <instrumentAssignment arrangementId="4" isEnabled="true">
      <instrument type="blue.orchestra.BlueSynthBuilder" enabled="true" editEnabled="true">
        <name>JNO60</name>
        <comment>oct range for frequencies: 4.35 - 14.35 (10 octaves)
Juno chorus: 2 x MN3009 BBD (256 stages, 128 cells, 4.10 ms @ 31250 Hz).
Modes I/II: triangle LFO, 0.5/0.8 Hz, 180 deg between channels
(Anwander; SoundForce Chorus 6). I+II: sine in phase, 1 Hz/8% (Juno 60)
or 8 Hz/25% (Juno 6); the original hardware has no combined mode
(Juno-106 OM), and Arturia's shortened I+II delay is not modelled.
Filters: poles measured on a real Juno-60 by Holters/Parker DAFx-18,
Table 1. BBD line: BLEP correction per Gabrielli/D'Angelo/Squartini
DAFx-25 (after D'Angelo's bbd_blep.m). Encode/hiss: Raffel/Smith
DAFx-10 sections 3.2/4.3. Min clock 26 kHz per Holters/Parker.</comment>
        <globalOrc />
        <globalSco />
        <instrumentText>ifreq = cpsmidinn(p4)
iamp = ampdbfs(p5)


// SLIDER VALUES

; LFO rate and delay calibrated in the shared output stage.

; LFO delay/trigger gain is shared in the always-on stage.

; DCO LFO: raw hardware captures give ~225 cents at 10, ~95 at 5.
; TR22/IC13 current control has a silicon-junction knee near 0.6V.
; ponytail: 60mV soft knee; refine with isolated low-depth hardware captures.
; Keep a small continuous response below the knee and exact zero at slider 0.
kPitchVoltage = limit(&lt;dco_lfo&gt;/2, 0, 5)
kPitchCents = (225*.06/4.4) * (log(1+exp((kPitchVoltage-.6)/.06)) - log(1+exp(-10)))

; Sub-Osc &amp; Noise Level: 0 to 100% (Logarithmic/Audio Taper)
kSubLevel   = ampdbfs(&lt;dco_sub&gt; * 6 - 60) ; Map 0-10 to -60 to 0 dB
kNoiseLevel = ampdbfs(&lt;dco_noise&gt; * 6 - 60)


; VCF Resonance: 0 to Self-Oscillation (Linear)
kResonance = &lt;vcf_res&gt; / 10
kQ = 0.5 + kResonance * 24.5 ;; range .5 - 25 (self-osc at 25), zdfladder

; VCF ENV: TR36 PNP, R21 1k + R135 12k + nominal VR12 5k.
; 2SA1015 typical 25C curve: Vbe ~.57V at Ic=.1mA, beta=200.
; Normalize current at 5V; full 12-oct gain is still provisional.
kEnvVoltage = 5 * limit(&lt;vcf_env&gt; / 10, 0, 1)
kEnvPrevious init -1
kEnvJunction init 0
kEnvModOct init 0
if kEnvVoltage != kEnvPrevious then
  kEnvJunction = min(kEnvVoltage, .6)
  kEnvIteration = 0
  while kEnvIteration &lt; 8 do
    kEnvExp = exp(kEnvJunction / .02569257912108585)
    kEnvJunction -= (kEnvJunction + 18000 * 2.3290119196933e-14 * (kEnvExp - 1) - kEnvVoltage) / \
                    (1 + 18000 * 2.3290119196933e-14 * kEnvExp / .02569257912108585)
    kEnvIteration += 1
  od
  kEnvModOct = 12 * limit((kEnvVoltage - kEnvJunction) / 4.407122102389906, 0, 1)
  kEnvPrevious = kEnvVoltage
endif

; VCF LFO: reuse the DCO soft knee with separate +/-3.46-octave gain.
; ponytail: provisional fit at 2.5/5/7.5; refine with isolated hardware CVs.
; Cache the nonlinear mapping until the live slider changes.
kLfoVoltage = limit(&lt;vcf_lfo&gt;/2, 0, 5)
kLfoPrevious init -1
kLfoModOct init 0
if kLfoVoltage != kLfoPrevious then
  kLfoModOct = (3.46*.06/4.4) * (log(1+exp((kLfoVoltage-.6)/.06)) - log(1+exp(-10)))
  kLfoPrevious = kLfoVoltage
endif



; --- JUNO-106 VCA LEVEL MAPPING ---
; kin_vca_level: Input from slider (0.0 to 10.0)
; Panel Marking -5 (0.0) to +5 (10.0), with 0 (5.0) as nominal.

; 1. Convert 0-10 slider to a -5 to +5 bipolar value
kBipolar = &lt;vca_level_adjust&gt; - 5

; 2. Define the dB range (e.g., +/- 12dB)
; 12 / 5 = 2.4 dB per panel unit
kDbOffset = kBipolar * 2.4

; 3. Convert dB to a linear gain multiplier
; ampdbfs(0) = 1.0 (No change at panel '0')
; ampdbfs(12) approx 3.98 (Boost at panel '+5')
; ampdbfs(-12) approx 0.25 (Cut at panel '-5')
kVcaPatchGain = ampdbfs(kDbOffset)

; Envelope Attack: 1 ms to 3 seconds (cubic in slider position)
iEnvA = 0.001 + (3.0 - 0.001) * pow(i(&lt;env_attack&gt;) / 10, 3)

; Envelope Decay: 2 ms to 12 seconds (cubic in slider position)
iEnvD = 0.002 + (12.0 - 0.002) * pow(i(&lt;env_decay&gt;) / 10, 3)

; Envelope Sustain: 0 to 100% (Linear)
iEnvS = i(&lt;env_sustain&gt;) / 10

; Envelope Release: 2 ms to 12 seconds (cubic in slider position)
iEnvR = 0.002 + (12.0 - 0.002) * pow(i(&lt;env_release&gt;) / 10, 3)


tigoto skipInit

// MAIN SIGNAL PROCESSING
Sjno60Lfo = "jno60_lfo_4"
; Publish the actual voice ID; Blue assigns a different ID to the output stage.
chnset int(p1), "jno60_voice_id_4"
kLfoVal chnget Sjno60Lfo
kLfoGain chnget "jno60_lfo_gain_4"
kLfoMod chnget "jno60_lfo_mod_4"
klfo = kLfoMod * kLfoGain
; Raw ENV Attack: -1 curve supported by hardware PWM captures; D/R provisional.
aEnv = transegr:a(0, iEnvA, -1, 1, iEnvD, -4.2, iEnvS, iEnvR, -4.2, 0)

asig = 0

kFreq = ifreq * cent(klfo * kPitchCents)

if(&lt;dco_saw_enabled&gt; == 1) then
  asig = vco2(1, kFreq)
endif

if(&lt;dco_pulse_enabled&gt; == 1) then
  kPwmWidth init 0
  kPwmDepth = (&lt;dco_pwm&gt; / 10) * 0.45

  ;; Source modes: LFO = 0, MAN = 1, ENV = 2
  if(&lt;dco_pwm_source&gt; == 0) then
    kPwmWidth = 0.5 + (kPwmDepth * kLfoVal)
  elseif(&lt;dco_pwm_source&gt; == 1) then
    kPwmWidth = 0.5 + kPwmDepth
  else
    kPwmWidth = 0.5 + k(aEnv) * kPwmDepth
  endif
  
  ; PWM Depth: 50% (Square) to 95% (Pulse)
  asig += vco2(1, kFreq, 2, kPwmWidth)
endif

if(&lt;dco_sub_enabled&gt; == 1) then
  asig += vco2(kSubLevel, kFreq * 0.5, 10)
endif

if(&lt;dco_noise_enabled&gt; == 1) then
  asig += random:a(-1, 1) * kNoiseLevel
endif

;; highpass: mode 0 boosts bass, mode 1 bypasses, mode 2 and 3 hpf)
if(&lt;hpf_mode&gt; == 0) then
  asig = pareq(asig, 70, ampdbfs(3), sqrt(.5), 1)
elseif(&lt;hpf_mode&gt; == 2) then
  asig = zdf2pole(asig, 225, 0.5, 1)
elseif(&lt;hpf_mode&gt; == 3) then
  asig = zdf2pole(asig, 700, 0.5, 1)
endif


;; VCF
;; cutoff (Hz) = 7.8 * 2^(freq + keytrack + env + lfo) in octaves
acut init 0
kcut_freq = (&lt;vcf_freq&gt; / 10) * 16.6667 ;; svc. manual 8-2: FREQ=3 -&gt; 248Hz
kcut_kybd = (&lt;vcf_kybd&gt; / 10) * (octcps(ifreq) - 8) ;; 8-3/8-4: ref = middle C
kcut = kcut_freq + kcut_kybd + (klfo * kLfoModOct)



acut_env = aEnv * kEnvModOct

if(&lt;vcf_invert&gt; == 1) then
  acut = -acut_env
else
  acut = acut_env
endif

acutoff = limit(7.8 * exp(0.6931472 * limit(acut + kcut, -10, 14)), 0, 0.49 * sr) ;; 7.8Hz * 2^oct, capped below Nyquist (zdfladder needs fc &lt; sr/2)
asig = zdfladder(asig, acutoff, kQ)

;; VCA
;; 0 = env, 1 = gate

asig *= iamp * kVcaPatchGain
if(i(&lt;vca_mode&gt;) == 0) then
  ; Reduced C9 control network: direct feedthrough plus a 10.78ms pole.
  ; TR6 loading/offset and the IR3R01 curve remain provisional.
  aEnvPole = tone(aEnv, sr/(6.283185307179586)*cosinv(2-cosh(1/(sr*.01078))))
  aVca = (12/49)*aEnv + (37/49)*aEnvPole
  xtratim(iEnvR + .15)
else
  ; C9=.22uF: charge via 5.6k || 22k, discharge via 22k.
  ; Exponential segments truncate at 14 tau (residual below 1ppm).
  iGateOn = .22e-6 / (1/5600 + 1/22000)
  iGateOff = .22e-6 * 22000
  aVca = transegr:a(0, 14*iGateOn, -14, 1, 14*iGateOff, -14, 0)
endif
asig *= aVca


blueMixerOut asig, asig

skipInit:</instrumentText>
        <alwaysOnInstrumentText>aLeft, aRight	blueMixerIn
; Andy Harman's isolated Juno-60 captures: panel 2.5/5/7.5/10.
; Keep 0.3Hz nominal minimum: the short rate-0 take has no complete cycle.
; ponytail: interpolate sparse anchors; refine with intermediate hardware takes.
iJno60Rates[] fillarray .3, .8414, 3.4147, 11.6442, 22.1067
kJno60RatePosition = limit(&lt;lfo_rate&gt;/2.5, 0, 4)
kJno60RateIndex = min(int(kJno60RatePosition), 3)
kJno60RateFraction = kJno60RatePosition - kJno60RateIndex
kJno60Rate = iJno60Rates[kJno60RateIndex] * pow(iJno60Rates[kJno60RateIndex+1]/iJno60Rates[kJno60RateIndex], kJno60RateFraction)
kJno60Lfo = lfo:k(1, kJno60Rate, 1)
Sjno60Lfo = "jno60_lfo_4"
chnset kJno60Lfo, Sjno60Lfo
; IC14 rounds the triangle for DCO/VCF; PWM takes raw TP17 instead.
; tanh(2*triangle) fits the isolated DCO capture (~3% normalized RMS error).
kJno60Mod = tanh(2*kJno60Lfo)/tanh(2)
chnset kJno60Mod, "jno60_lfo_mod_4"

; Owner's manual p.17: AUTO delays the first key of a non-legato phrase;
; MANUAL fades in from the trigger press and stops on release. PWM stays raw.
kJno60VoiceId chnget "jno60_voice_id_4"
kJno60Held active kJno60VoiceId, 0, 1
kJno60Mode = (&lt;lfo_trigger_mode&gt; &lt; .5 ? 0 : 1)
kJno60Gate = (kJno60Mode == 0 ? (kJno60VoiceId &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; kJno60Held &gt; 0 ? 1 : 0) : &lt;lfo_trig&gt;)
kJno60Age init 0
kJno60PreviousGate init 0
kJno60PreviousMode init -1
if kJno60Gate == 0 || kJno60PreviousGate == 0 || kJno60Mode != kJno60PreviousMode then
  kJno60Age = 0
else
  kJno60Age += 1/kr
endif
kJno60PreviousGate = kJno60Gate
kJno60PreviousMode = kJno60Mode
; Seconds measured relative to note onset, not the start of the WAV file.
; This hardware unit has a ~2.5s max hold; service calibration specifies 2s.
iJno60Delays[] fillarray 0, .061, .406, 1.038, 2.505
iJno60Fades[] fillarray 0, .047, .213, .557, 1.347
kJno60DelayPosition = limit(&lt;lfo_delay_time&gt;/2.5, 0, 4)
kJno60DelayIndex = min(int(kJno60DelayPosition), 3)
kJno60DelayFraction = kJno60DelayPosition - kJno60DelayIndex
kJno60Delay = iJno60Delays[kJno60DelayIndex] + kJno60DelayFraction*(iJno60Delays[kJno60DelayIndex+1]-iJno60Delays[kJno60DelayIndex])
kJno60Fade = iJno60Fades[kJno60DelayIndex] + kJno60DelayFraction*(iJno60Fades[kJno60DelayIndex+1]-iJno60Fades[kJno60DelayIndex])
if kJno60Mode == 0 then
  kJno60Gain = (kJno60Delay == 0 ? 1 : kJno60Gate * limit((kJno60Age-kJno60Delay)/max(kJno60Fade, 1/kr), 0, 1))
else
  ; ponytail: MANUAL fade duration uses delay anchors; no isolated MANUAL take yet.
  kJno60Gain = (kJno60Delay == 0 ? kJno60Gate : kJno60Gate * limit(kJno60Age/kJno60Delay, 0, 1))
endif
chnset kJno60Gain, "jno60_lfo_gain_4"


if(&lt;chorus_mode&gt; &gt; 0) then
  a1, a2 = juno_chorus(aLeft, &lt;chorus_mode&gt;, .01)
else
  a1 = aLeft
  a2 = aRight
endif

; OUTPUT

blueMixerOut a1, a2</alwaysOnInstrumentText>
